+## S10. Table 8 contributing-fit diagnostics
+
+For each pooled comparison, a diagnostic flag means that at least one positively weighted subgroup fit for either dose triggered that diagnostic. The point flag and number of flagged bootstrap draws out of 999 are reported separately. The proportional analysis was freshly refitted with opening risk sets supplied to the diagnostic routine. For the forced-alpha sensitivity, the same routine and survivor-model prediction were evaluated at the archived fitted parameters on the original matched death histories; 300 fresh matched refits independently reproduced the archived parameters, points and all diagnostic flags exactly. No draw was excluded, and all reported Table 8 point estimates and percentile intervals are unchanged.
+
+Table: Table 8 diagnostic flags by comparison. Point flag / number of draws (out of 999). {#tbl:si_table8_diagnostics}
