+For every comparison, the point flags and draw counts for insufficient signal, unavailable residual screen, upper frailty bound, baseline-rate bound, weak identification, insufficient deaths, failed fit and legacy relative-error screen were zero. The raw gap-clamp indicator records any nonpositive reconstructed offset; it is not the material-deficit assumption diagnostic in Section 2.5. Residual-screen flags are exploratory model-discrepancy indicators, not calibrated global goodness-of-fit tests or criteria for discarding resamples. Source: `analysis/table8_diagnostics/` (full subgroup and comparison flag arrays, category counts, and fresh-refit verification).
